WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.932
A secure Razor Pages baseline starts with
reviewable organization.

2
00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:17.109
Pages, folders, handlers, and conventions
should help the team see which workflows

3
00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:23.596
are public, which require identity, which
require policy,

4
00:00:23.676 --> 00:00:27.392
and which modify important state.

5
00:00:27.472 --> 00:00:36.314
The application should not depend on
hidden structure or memory to explain access

6
00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:37.162
rules.

7
00:00:37.242 --> 00:00:45.059
Authenticate users explicitly and
authorize pages, folders, records,

8
00:00:45.139 --> 00:00:49.111
and sensitive actions on the server.

9
00:00:49.191 --> 00:00:53.676
User interface behavior can guide users,

10
00:00:53.756 --> 00:00:59.265
but server-side handlers own the access
decision.

11
00:00:59.345 --> 00:01:07.931
For record-specific workflows, the handler
should verify ownership, tenant,

12
00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:15.186
workflow state, or permission against
trusted server-side data.

13
00:01:15.266 --> 00:01:23.723
Protect state-changing browser forms with
antiforgery validation and clear

14
00:01:23.803 --> 00:01:26.366
request-intent rules.

15
00:01:26.446 --> 00:01:32.340
Keep GET-style requests for safe retrieval
behavior.

16
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:38.442
Review custom forms, AJAX submissions,
partial views,

17
00:01:38.522 --> 00:01:47.748
and nonstandard handlers so they receive
the same protection as conventional forms.

18
00:01:47.828 --> 00:01:51.160
Treat bound data as untrusted.

19
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.237
Use input models to define what a page
accepts,

20
00:01:56.317 --> 00:02:02.724
validate required fields and business
rules on the server,

21
00:02:02.804 --> 00:02:06.392
and update only intended fields.

22
00:02:06.472 --> 00:02:13.903
Use Razor output encoding correctly, avoid
unnecessary raw output,

23
00:02:13.983 --> 00:02:22.056
and handle user-generated content
according to its destination context.

24
00:02:22.136 --> 00:02:26.877
Finally, review the operational baseline.

25
00:02:26.957 --> 00:02:34.389
Cookies, session, TempData, uploads,
static files, logs, secrets,

26
00:02:34.469 --> 00:02:39.851
errors, dependencies, HTTPS, security
headers,

27
00:02:39.931 --> 00:02:47.106
and production configuration all shape
real application safety.

28
00:02:47.186 --> 00:02:53.849
Secure Razor Pages development is not
about adding ceremony.

29
00:02:53.929 --> 00:03:00.592
It is about making critical decisions
explicit, consistent,

30
00:03:00.672 --> 00:03:04.260
and ready for production review.
